sequenceDiagram
  participant C as Retained Codex controller
  participant H as Canonical host (vcp-lifecycle foundation)
  participant S as Canonical store + ledger
  participant P as HTTP transport / provider
  C->>H: work admission for HTTP attempt (root, helper, compaction, child)
  H->>S: capture final request body artifact
  H->>S: reserve shared funds + record send intent
  H->>P: send request
  P-->>H: response stream
  H->>S: capture full response bytes before parsing/display limits
  H->>S: settle usage or retain unknown liability
  H-->>C: parsed response
  Note over H,S: capture failure fences work · owner loss pauses<br/>tasks · reopen keeps uncertain effects/charges, no<br/>automatic replay
